# Far copy, step 26.3 (7.2.44): the answerer. One program of language 3, nothing new: data, array, lut, store, lt, if, key, emit, copy.
# It serves a window of 8 cells of 8 bits (the array win) over its stdin/stdout: the answers go to stdout, so the shell must connect the
# stdout of the asker to this stdin and this stdout to the stdin of the asker.
# The record of a request: fixed size, 6 bytes, read by three `key`:   op (8 bits)   pos (32 bits)   dat (8 bits)
#   op = 0  stop (no answer)      op bit 0 = 1 (op = 1)  get: answer one byte, win[pos]      op bit 1 = 1 (op = 2)  put: win[pos] = dat (no answer)
#   a number is stored as `key` stores it: the first bit of the stream is the lowest bit (pos: 4 bytes, the lowest byte first).
#   pos is the number of a byte; out of the window (pos >= 8): get answers a byte of ones (255) = the prohibitive price; put changes nothing.
#   The end of the stdin (the channel is closed) is a stop: op is zeroed before every read and a read at EOF leaves it as it was.
# pos is 32 bits (7.2.44, 26.4: the copy `copy &x 0x2...` of the pass l4c makes the requests, the byte number is the bit position / 8): lt works over 8 nibbles
# (c3 is 9 bits, the test is c3[8]); the index stays pos[0:3] (the window has 8 cells). A bigger window: the array and the index width (K up to 10).
:op data 8 0
:pos data 32 0
:dat data 8 0
:ans data 8 0
:zero8 data 8 0
:ones data 8 255
:eight data 32 8
:c3 data 9 0
:win array 3 8
:init data 64 "COPYMACH"
:i0 data 3 0
:i1 data 3 1
:i2 data 3 2
:i3 data 3 3
:i4 data 3 4
:i5 data 3 5
:i6 data 3 6
:i7 data 3 7
:main block
store &win &i0 &init[0:8]
store &win &i1 &init[8:16]
store &win &i2 &init[16:24]
store &win &i3 &init[24:32]
store &win &i4 &init[32:40]
store &win &i5 &init[40:48]
store &win &i6 &init[48:56]
store &win &i7 &init[56:64]
goto &loop
:loop block
copy &op &zero8
key &op
key &pos
key &dat
lt &pos &eight &c3
if &op[0] &get &notget
:get block
if &c3[8] &getin &getout
:getin block
lut &win &pos[0:3] &ans
emit &ans
goto &loop
:getout block
emit &ones
goto &loop
:notget block
if &op[1] &put &done
:put block
if &c3[8] &putin &loop
:putin block
store &win &pos[0:3] &dat
goto &loop
:done block
halt
